{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Algorithmic Bias.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Algorithmic Bias.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"algorithmic bias algorithmic bias","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Algorithmic Bias.md","fileName":"Algorithmic Bias.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Algorithmic Bias","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Algorithmic Fairness and Justice]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algorithmic Fairness and Justice","Data Science Pipeline","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Algorithmic Bias.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Algorithmic Bias.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"algorithmic bias algorithmic bias","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Algorithmic Bias.md","fileName":"Algorithmic Bias.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Algorithmic Bias","heading":"Algorithmic Bias","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Algorithmic bias is a systematic tendency for an automated system to produce distorted or unequally harmful outcomes. Bias can enter through the population sampled, labels, variables, model objective, deployment data, or the way people interpret and act on the output.\n\nThe source is not always a prejudiced programmer. A model trained on historical practice may accurately reproduce an unjust pattern, and an apparently neutral variable may act as a social proxy. Because bias can emerge throughout the [[Data Science Pipeline]], mitigation requires technical testing together with judgment about which differences are ethically relevant.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algorithmic Fairness and Justice","Data Science Pipeline","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Algorithmic Bias.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/